## Core product

Phase 3 of the thin API migration. The frontend stops knowing anything about AI prompts. Every synchronous text action (brainstorm, expand, compress, clarify, simplify, tldr, bullets, rewrite) gets a dedicated, action-named backend route under `/api/text/`. Each route is a thin Python facade that invokes a SKILL.md-backed skill. Prompt strings are deleted from TypeScript and centralized in SKILL.md files. The frontend `ai.service.ts` becomes a 30-line wrapper with no instruction strings.

## Architectural principle — facade

The API is a facade. The frontend has zero prompt strings, zero system instructions, zero AI behavior knowledge. It sends `{ text, ...params }`, receives `{ text, latencyMs }`. Every AI decision lives in SKILL.md. Python routes are ~10 lines: auth, extract body, call skill, return response.

## Target API contract

All text operations grouped under `/api/text/`:

```
POST /api/text/brainstorm  { text, question?, context? }  → { text, latencyMs }
POST /api/text/expand      { text }                        → { text, latencyMs }
POST /api/text/compress    { text }                        → { text, latencyMs }
POST /api/text/clarify     { text }                        → { text, latencyMs }
POST /api/text/simplify    { text }                        → { text, latencyMs }
POST /api/text/tldr        { text }                        → { text, latencyMs }
POST /api/text/bullets     { text }                        → { text, latencyMs }
POST /api/text/rewrite     { text, style }                 → { text, latencyMs }
```

`style` values for `/rewrite`: `Concise | Technical | Executive | Narrative | Punchy`. The backend maps each style to Claude instructions inside `rewrite/SKILL.md`. The frontend never sees the mapping.

